cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "HARAM-VLM: Look Closer Only When Needed"
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite it as below. It accompanies a manuscript
  currently under review; the venue and DOI will be added once that concludes.
type: software
abstract: >-
  A training-free, model-agnostic predict-then-allocate controller for
  vision-language models. A cheap low-resolution scout pass answers a query and
  estimates its own reliability; only uncertain queries are escalated to a
  high-resolution pass. The controller is a single threshold on the scout's
  confidence, adds no parameters, and wraps any frozen VLM. This repository also
  releases a clean, scalable, image-disjoint COCO-to-POPE evaluation protocol
  that removes the ~93 percent train-test contamination present in POPE-style
  fine-tuning.
